OVERVIEW: Extract Hounsfield Unit values from CT images

USAGE: dicom-measure hu <file-path> [--output <output>] [--format <format>] [--unit <unit>] [--force] [--verbose] [--point <point>] [--rect <rect>] [--statistics]

ARGUMENTS:
  <file-path>             Path to the DICOM file

OPTIONS:
  -o, --output <output>   Output file path (prints to stdout if omitted)
  -f, --format <format>   Output format: text, json, csv (values: text, json,
                          csv; default: text)
  --unit <unit>           Unit for measurements: mm, cm, um, inches, pixels
                          (physical units need a pixel spacing; see the
                          overview) (values: mm, cm, um, inches, pixels;
                          default: mm)
  --force                 Force parsing of files without DICM prefix
  --verbose               Verbose output for debugging
  --point <point>         Point to sample as x,y (e.g., 200,200)
  --rect <rect>           Rectangular ROI as x,y,width,height for averaging
  --statistics            Calculate extended statistics for ROI
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

